<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  «Пополнить» — the amount, and its confirm.

  REACHED FROM TWO PLACES AND IT IS ONE DIALOG: AccountFragment.showTopUpDialog is
  called by the «Пополнить» button under the ring and by the balance chip in the
  profile row, so this layout is what both of them open. There is no second copy to
  drift out of step with.

  WHY IT WAS «слишком толсто». Widget.Departament.TextField is the app's FILLED
  field — boxBackgroundColor colorSurfaceContainerHighest — and it carries
  errorEnabled, which reserves a caption line under the box whether or not there is
  ever an error to put in it. A filled 56dp slab plus a reserved error line, inside a
  24dp-padded dialog, was the heaviest object on a screen that asks for one number.
  The mass came from those three things and not from the height, which is the touch
  floor and stays.

  WHAT IT IS NOW, in the account's own language: a CONTOUR, no fill, radius_control
  16, stroke_frame 1.5dp — the same 1.5 the two buttons on the tab draw and the same
  1.5 «Оплатить» draws — and no reserved error line. The typography is the ramp's:
  the amount is TextAppearance.App.Numeric.Money, which is the role every ₽ figure
  in the product already takes (Space Grotesk, tabular figures), instead of the
  16sp hardcoded on the shared EditText style.

  Colours are attributes only: ?attr/colorOnSurface for the value,
  ?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant for the placeholder, @color/field_stroke_selector for
  the boundary (accent on focus, colorOutlineControl at rest — the 3:1 component
  boundary, not the hairline). ThemeOverlay.Mono can reach all of them.

  THE CONFIRM IS IN THE DIALOG, not in the AlertDialog's button bar, and it is the
  account's ONE button shape: 48dp, radius_button 24, accent contour, no fill —
  «Пополнить» on the tab, «Оплатить» on the buy screen and this are now one control
  drawn three times. «Отмена» is the same shape with the quiet label, so the pair
  reads like §5's «Пополнить»/«Продлить» row rather than like a system dialog.

  The dialog's own corner stays @drawable/bg_dialog's 20dp: that is the app-wide
  dialog surface, shared by every AlertDialog in the product, and giving this one
  screen its own radius would be the inconsistency the request is about.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingHorizontal="@dimen/screen_gutter"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/space_8"
    android:paddingBottom="@dimen/space_4">

    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
        android:id="@+id/til_top_up"
        style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        app:boxBackgroundColor="@android:color/transparent"
        app:boxStrokeWidth="@dimen/stroke_frame"
        app:errorEnabled="false">

        <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
            android:id="@+id/et_top_up"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField.EditText"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:hint="@string/account_top_up_hint"
            android:imeOptions="actionDone"
            android:inputType="numberDecimal"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric.Money"
            android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurface" />
    </com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_16"
        android:baselineAligned="false"
        android:orientation="horizontal">

        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/btn_top_up_cancel"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/btn_height"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:minWidth="0dp"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/space_8"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_8"
            android:text="@android:string/cancel"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Button"
            android:textColor="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant"
            app:cornerRadius="@dimen/radius_button"
            app:strokeColor="?attr/colorOutlineControl"
            app:strokeWidth="@dimen/stroke_frame" />

        <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
            android:id="@+id/btn_top_up_confirm"
            style="@style/Widget.Departament.Button.Tertiary"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/btn_height"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_8"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:minWidth="0dp"
            android:paddingStart="@dimen/space_8"
            android:paddingEnd="@dimen/space_8"
            android:text="@string/account_top_up"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Button"
            app:cornerRadius="@dimen/radius_button"
            app:strokeColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
            app:strokeWidth="@dimen/stroke_frame" />
    </LinearLayout>
</LinearLayout>
